# Bootstrap questionnaire — {{ project_name }}

Every decision this project must make before its standards are binding. It works with any AI
tool or with none: answer in `.baseline/answers.yaml` (same ids), then apply the answers to the
documents named in **Writes to**. Paths in this file are relative to `docs/`.

How to answer each question: `default`, a value, or `later`. `later` is always allowed. The
question is then recorded in `docs/DECISION-QUEUE.md` and is never guessed. **An answer equal to
the default is an answer; only an explicit `later` leaves `[[...]]` in a document.**

Questions are asked **one phase at a time**, numbered, with the recommended default and its
trade-off. A phase is finished when every question in it is answered or deferred. A phase with
more than about 25 items is split into numbered batches.

**Order:** 0 → 1 → 2 → 3 → **4P (packs)** → 4 → 5 → 6. Packs come before phase 4 because a
pack's `PACK.md` `amends:` list names core documents it changes; each amendment is applied to the
amended document *before* that document is offered in its own phase.

**Component kinds scope everything.** Question 0.5 records what the product consists of and what
kind each component is: `service` (request/response network service), `daemon` (long-running
process without request/response), `cli` (command-line program), `library` (code consumed by
other code), `ui` (an interface a person uses), `batch` (a job or pipeline that runs and ends).
A later question that concerns only kinds the product lacks is skipped, and a rule that applies
only to some kinds carries an `_(applies to: …)_` tag. A document whose `applies-to` kinds are all
absent may be set `status: not-applicable` with a `reason:`.

**A pointer is an answer once its target is.** A rule that says "decided in `13-technology/`"
counts as answered when the matching area is answered, or explicitly deferred, in phase 5. Until
then a document that points there is not ratified.

The rows below are the **headline** questions. Every document also has a `## Parameters` table;
its remaining open parameters are offered in the same phase as one bulk list — "accept all
defaults, or name the ones to change". `node scripts/params.mjs <path>` prints that list for the
documents a phase writes to.

Answer ids in `.baseline/answers.yaml`: `<question id>` for a headline question (`1.3`), and
`<question id>/<doc path>/<param>` for a bulk parameter (`4.2/06-security/authn-authz.md/actor_types`).

