## Phase 4 — Platform defaults

Each core document from layers 05–12 is offered as a whole: **accept** its proposed defaults,
**change** named parameters, or **later**. Changes become ADRs when they have a real alternative.
A document whose `applies-to` kinds are absent from 0.5 is offered as `not-applicable` with a
reason. `13-technology/README.md` is not here: it closes phase 5.

| Id | Document | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 4.1 | `05-protocols/*` | accept |
| 4.2 | `06-security/*` — always confirm `data_classes` and `agent_dependency_changes` explicitly, and the actors in `authn-authz.md` (`actor_types`: user, operator, service, system, agent; an operator is vendor personnel) | accept |
| 4.3 | `07-observability/*` | accept |
| 4.4 | `08-reliability/*` | accept |
| 4.5 | `09-errors/taxonomy.md` | accept |
| 4.6 | `10-patterns/*` | accept |
| 4.7 | `11-style/*` | accept |
| 4.8 | `12-testing/*` | accept |

